  "Question": "How many positive factors of \\(36\\) are also multiples of \\(4?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(3\\)",
    "C": "\\(4\\)",
    "D": "\\(5\\)",
    "E": "\\(6\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Every factor pair of \\(36\\) has a member at most \\(6\\), since two numbers greater than \\(6\\) would have a product greater than \\(36\\). Testing \\(1\\) through \\(6\\) gives all the pairs:\n\\[\n1\\times36,\\quad 2\\times18,\\quad 3\\times12,\\quad 4\\times9,\\quad 6\\times6.\n\\]\nAmong the factors in these pairs, exactly \\(4,12,36\\) are multiples of \\(4\\). There are \\(3\\), so the answer is \\(\\boxed{3}\\), choice B.",
